            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="1018" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/423: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-23T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                                1926—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 23—9:45
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>507. Department’s 240, October 22nd. In expressing preference for draft formula
                    set forth in my 462, October 8th and 477, October 14th, am I to understand that
                    Department is unwilling to join in draft formula presented in paragraph 2 of my
                    497, October 20th?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
